# MAILCHIMP MERGE TAG RULES

## WHY THIS SKILL EXISTS
A live campaign once went out with the greeting
written as *|FNAME|**|ELSE|*there. Mailchimp only
understands *|ELSE|* inside a complete conditional
block, so every recipient saw the literal text:
Froggy*|ELSE|*there —
in their inbox. This skill exists so that never
happens again. No exceptions, no shortcuts.

## THE ONE APPROVED GREETING
Use exactly this pattern for every greeting that
falls back when the first name is missing:

*|IF:FNAME|*Hey *|FNAME|* —*|ELSE|*Hey there —*|END:IF|*

Adjust the wording (Hey/Hi/Morning) as the campaign
requires, but the tag structure is fixed:
IF opens it, ELSE splits it, END:IF closes it.
All three tags must be present or none of them.

## HARD RULES
RULE 1 — *|ELSE|* is NEVER valid on its own. It only
works between *|IF:...|* and *|END:IF|*. A bare
*|ELSE|* prints as literal text in the email.

RULE 2 — Every *|IF:...|* must have a matching
*|END:IF|* in the same block of copy. Unclosed
conditionals print as literal text.

RULE 3 — Never split a merge tag across HTML tags.
Editors sometimes wrap parts of a tag in <span> or
<strong>. A tag like *|FN<span>AME|*</span> will not
merge. Keep each full tag inside one text node.

RULE 4 — Merge tags are case sensitive and use
straight pipes and asterisks: *|FNAME|*. Never use
smart quotes, spaces inside the tag, or lowercase
field names.

RULE 5 — Simpler is safer. If a fallback greeting is
needed and conditionals feel risky, set a default
value of "there" on the FNAME merge field in the
audience settings and write the greeting as:
Hey *|FNAME|* —
Mailchimp fills the default automatically when the
field is empty. This is the preferred approach for
all DBW rep campaigns.

## MANDATORY PREFLIGHT SCAN
Before saving a campaign as draft and again before
any send step, scan the complete final HTML and
subject line and confirm every check below. If any
check fails: STOP. Fix the HTML. Re-scan. Do not
save or send until all checks pass.

CHECK 1 — Search the HTML for the string *|ELSE|*.
For every occurrence, confirm an *|IF: appears
before it and an *|END:IF|* appears after it in the
same conditional block. A bare *|ELSE|* is an
automatic hard stop.

CHECK 2 — Count *|IF: occurrences and *|END:IF|*
occurrences. The counts must be equal.

CHECK 3 — List every merge tag in the HTML (every
substring starting *| and ending |*). Each must be
a tag Mailchimp actually supports, spelled exactly:
*|FNAME|* *|LNAME|* *|EMAIL|* *|IF:...|* *|ELSE|*
*|ELSEIF:...|* *|END:IF|* *|UNSUB|* *|ARCHIVE|*
*|LIST:COMPANY|* *|HTML:...|* or another documented
Mailchimp tag. Anything unrecognized is a hard stop.

CHECK 4 — Confirm no merge tag is interrupted by an
HTML element (see RULE 3). View the raw HTML source,
not the rendered preview, to verify.

CHECK 5 — Send-to-self test when possible. If the
workflow supports a test send, send one to
jfgreco84@gmail.com and confirm the greeting renders
as a real name or the fallback — never raw tag text —
before the real send.

## SCOPE
These rules apply to every email built for DBW or
Best Solution through any workflow: rep campaign
blasts, one-off sends, test campaigns, everything.
They apply to subject lines and preview text as well
as body HTML.
